codex
1. Changed the fast-engine serialization entry points so they serialize the graph object they were actually passed, instead of calling `App.serializeGraphData()` with no argument. I applied that in [engine-fast-worker-host.js](/C:/Users/suzuk/AppData/Local/Temp/fact-sim-auto-patch/1773514136949-5572/js/app/engine-fast-worker-host.js#L59), [engine-fast-par-host.js](/C:/Users/suzuk/AppData/Local/Temp/fact-sim-auto-patch/1773514136949-5572/js/app/engine-fast-par-host.js#L30), and [engine-fast-par-partitioner.js](/C:/Users/suzuk/AppData/Local/Temp/fact-sim-auto-patch/1773514136949-5572/js/app/engine-fast-par-partitioner.js#L18). In the parallel host and partitioner paths I also aligned serialization with the worker path by preserving stop-group metadata during fallback serialization. No protected `dt` or `event` engine files were modified.

2. Verification run: `fact-sim-ai engine_test` with `engines=["event-fast","event-fast-worker","event-fast-par"]`, examples `["simple","branch","sample_line1","sample_line2","shuttle_line5","carrier_config","pallet_station_demo"]`, `reruns=0`, `strictFinalParity=false`, `stopOnFirstFailure=false`, `targetSimMs=30000`, `maxWallMs=2500`, `realStepMs=16`. Result: `PASS`, `32/32` cases passed, with `dt` retained as baseline and no failures or warnings.

3. Residual risk: the public engine suite stayed green, but the inferred failure was a graph-instance serialization bug that is most likely to show up when a non-current graph object is passed into fast worker/parallel runners. I fixed that seam directly, but I was not able to reproduce that exact hidden scenario end-to-end with the available harness.
